Hello,=0A=
=0A=
I wish to submit a specific BDF for this device.=0A=
=0A=
The device have two names: TP-Link Archer C6 v2 (US), and TP-Link Archer A6=
 v2 (US/TW). They are identical, and has been supported by OpenWRT since 20=
19. Unfortunately, the 5GHz radio suffers=A0from low RSSI. It seems that th=
e radio components were changed substantially that the stock values in boar=
d-2.bin doesn't work well with it. Replacing the default board file with th=
e one included in stock firmware fixes the 5GHz range.=0A=
=0A=
> description for what hardware this is=0A=
=0A=
It is a QCA9563 based board, consisting of one QCA9563 radio used for 2.4GH=
z WLAN, and one QCA9886 radio used for 5GHz WLAN.=0A=
=0A=
> origin of the board file (did you create it yourself or where you downloa=
ded)=0A=
=0A=
I pulled it off the latest stock firmware image, from '/lib/firmware/QCA988=
8/hw.2/boardData_2_0_QCA9888_5G_YA105_us.bin'.=0A=
=0A=
> ids to be used with the board file (ATH10K_BD_IE_BOARD_NAME in ath10k)=0A=
=0A=
I'd suggest:=0A=
bus=3Dpci,bmi-chip-id=3D0,bmi-board-id=3D24,variant=3Dtp-link-archer-c6-v2-=
us=0A=
=0A=
Which is based off the console log after I intentionally replaced the board=
-2.bin with an invalid one:=0A=
[   14.965856] ath10k_pci 0000:00:00.0: failed to fetch board data for bus=
=3Dpci,bmi-chip-id=3D0,bmi-board-id=3D24 from ath10k/QCA9888/hw2.0/board-2.=
bin=0A=
=0A=
> attach the actual board file (board.bin)=0A=
=0A=
As attached. I left the original file name as is.=0A=
=0A=
File name: boardData_2_0_QCA9888_5G_YA105_us.bin=0A=
sha256 sum: 10ef67f14bab5d565ce777f7c852124acbfe4cd7e04a06d548f110201553dd2=
5=0A=
=0A=
Thank you.=0A=
=0A=
Kind regards,=0A=
Adam E.=

